[Coordinates] =  cartesian
[ACSolver]    =  0
[Comment]     =  "Silicon Steel: fit to the fourteen DC magnetization curves of US Steel, Nonoriented Sheet Steel for Magnetic Applications, ADUSS 31-7103-01 (May 1978). Four-process model (reversible toe + Burr-XII knee + hard wall shoulder + Akulov-constrained rotation); silicon from the book's own resistivity via its p.116 formula; Js = 2.151 - 0.048 Si-eq (pure iron less the book's example 0.005 C and 0.25 Mn; Exner); K1(Si) from Bozorth Ferromagnetism Fig. 12-16 sets the rotation field scale, which the pages accept at no cost but do not pin. M-15 is not in the catalog: it is the composition law at the 50 uOhm-cm of the Cleveland-Cliffs DI-MAX bulletin (Si-eq 3.32), checked against Armco's 1984 DI-MAX M-15 sheet. B IS ON A NET-METAL BASIS: the catalog computes induction from specimen mass over assumed density, so the lamination factor is NOT in these curves, and LamFill is a suggested stacking factor by gauge (midpoint of the femm.info stacking-factor table: 0.955 at 14 mil, 0.965 at 18-18.5 mil, 0.975 at 24-25 mil) -- set your own if you know it. Sigma and d_lam are per grade from the book. Materials only, no geometry. See sicurves.pdf."
[PointProps]   = 0
[BdryProps]   = 0
